 would just say  you know table for four or whatever and  then there would be a discussion amongst  the hostess and maybe a waiter or  something like that about where it is  that they want to see us and there will  be some question as to whether we would  or wouldn't be ok in a certain spot like  do they want to sit outside or not and  then I'll just respond in Spanish and  say we actually would love to sit  outside and usually there's no  conversation in New York it's it's not  actually surprising to anybody so then  it's just kind of like oh ok yeah let's  just go outside and then only later  we'll do something  say oh you're speaking Spanish to us  yeah or something like that but the most  glaring one is that time at the laser  tag thing where the people were actually  calling me you know a prick or whatever  and I said a lot a lot of people speak  Spanish you got to be careful you ever  go to like a Mexican restaurant or a  Spanish restaurant and insist on  speaking Spanish and they think that  you're just some gringo trying to speak  it as a Second Language  no and they'll just revert right back to  English how does that work only time  that that has happened  so most native Spanish speakers would  identify that I speak Spanish and the  only time that it was different was I  think I've told the story before I once  went on vacation to one of the Balearic  Balearic I think is how you pronounce it  islands off the coast of Spain they're  Spanish islands and these islands are  very very heavily trafficked by both  British and German tourists and there  was a restaurant that I actually went to  that was a quote Spanish restaurant but  it was owned by a German woman and she  was she spoke Spanish as a second  language in other words she's German  she moved to Spain learn Spanish and  runs the Spanish restaurant I didn't  know that she was German because I'm in  Spain so I assumed when someone comes up  we're gonna be speaking in Spanish and  she assumed that I didn'